BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Author Talk - Black Film: A History of Black Representation and Pa
 rticipation in the Movies by David F Walker
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260609T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260609T193000
UID:6a07af61748daf857d58d270@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:See David F Walker discuss his new book\,\nBlack Film: A Histo
 ry of Black Representation and Participation\nin the Movies\n!  It is an e
 ngaging celebration of Black actors\, films\, and filmmakers\, as well as 
 an exploration of the social forces that informed the art and were transfo
 rmed by it.\nWalker is the Eisner Award-winning writer of\nThe Black Panth
 er Party: A Graphic Novel History\n\, co-creator of the Eisner Award-winni
 ng series\nBitter Root\n.\nThere will be a Q&A portion\, and books will be
  available for purchase and signing.
LOCATION:Aloha Community Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a07af61748daf857d58d270
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
