SUMMARY:Music at the Hearth: Ringdown
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260712T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260712T150000
UID:6a0f72174dc267647daa45ea@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What if Clara Schumann wrote pop songs? Collaborators Caroline
  Shaw and Danni Lee Parpan—who between the two of them have a Pulitzer P
 rize\, a handful of Grammys\, and a "Best Drum Major" Award—describe Rin
 gdown as an electronic cinematic pop duo based in Portland\, OR and New Yo
 rk\, NY. Others have described Ringdown as the love child of Johannes Brah
 ms and Brandi Carlile—if they were born in the same century and if Brahm
 s was a queer woman. Come hear them and decide for yourself.\nHeld at the 
 Library Hearth.
LOCATION:Tualatin Public Library\, Library Hearth
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a0f72174dc267647daa45ea
