BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Page Turners Book Club: The Anthropocene Reviewed
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260603T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260603T193000
UID:69f69afa8ddc1caf5f20b508@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this collection of bite-sized and snackable essays\, John G
 reen (bestselling author of\nEverything is Tuberculosis)\nexplores and rat
 es marvels of our world\, like Halley’s Comet and Dr. Pepper. Each piece
  showcases his endearing mix of humor and wisdom\, and illuminates larger 
 truths about seeing the world with curiosity and compassion.\nReserve it\n
 here\n:  Also available in eBook\, downloadable audiobook\, and audioboo
 k CD\nJoin online by clicking here:\nhttps://bit.ly/ACLbkclub\nOr call 253
 -215-8782 to join by phone.\nMeeting ID: 924 6989 8432 & Passcode: 037016\
 nIf you would like to read ahead\, here is the book club’s schedule for 
 the rest of 2026:\nJune 3rd (online) & 4th (in-person) - The Anthropocene 
 Reviewed\nhttps://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/record/S143C3867359\nby John 
 Green\nJuly - Break\nAugust - Break\nSeptember 9th (online) & 10th (in-per
 son) - Tress of the Emerald Sea\nhttps://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/record
 /S143C4189016\nby Brandon Sanderson\nOctober 7th (online) & 8th (in-person
 ) - Remarkably Bright Creatures\nhttps://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/record
 /S143C4054983\nby Shelby Van Pelt\nNovember 4th (online) & 5th (in-person)
  - Bad Cree\nhttps://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/record/S143C4157107\nby Je
 ssica Johns\nDecember - Break
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69f69afa8ddc1caf5f20b508
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
